        "statement": "There exists $a\\in S$ lying on the boundary of no finite graph language with initial set.\nLet $a^{(n)}$ be obtained from $a$ by changing its $n$th bit, and set\n\\[\n S_0=\\{a\\}\\cup\\{a^{(n)}:n\\in\\NN\\}.\n\\]\nFor every such language $L$, the intersection $L\\cap S_0$ is clopen in $S_0$.\nThe first-disagreement map\n\\[\n \\rho(s)=\\begin{cases}\\min\\{n:s(n)\\ne a(n)\\}&s\\ne a,\\\\\\infty&s=a\\end{cases}\n\\]\nis a continuous surjection $S\\to B$, and $\\rho|_{S_0}:S_0\\to B$ is a homeomorphism.",
